en the margin toward single digits low enough to make this a genuine tossup.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["No expert ratings published yet; forecast rests on fundamentals and polls.", "New or vacant seat with no expert ratings; fundamentals only.", "No usable general-election polls; forecast rests on fundamentals and expert ratings."]}, "overview": "Connecticut has voted Democratic in every presidential election since 1992, and its partisan lean sits about eight points toward Democrats relative to the nation. The 2028 race is open with the incumbent term-limited, so no incumbency advantage applies to either side. No general-election polls, expert ratings, or fundraising figures are available for this race yet, leaving the state's fundamentals as the main guide.\n\nThe forecast therefore expects the Democratic nominee to carry Connecticut by roughly eight points, consistent with recent presidential results under a neutral national environment. Uncertainty is wider than usual because no state polling exists. A strong national Republican wave could narrow the margin, while a favorable Democratic environment could push it toward the double-digit territory of recent cycles. The race is rated Lean Democratic.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.8243, "margin": 8.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.781, "margin": 8.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.7754, "margin": 8.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.7619, "margin": 8.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.7738, "margin": 8.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.7843, "margin": 8.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.7768, "margin": 8.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.7843, "margin": 8.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.7811, "margin": 8.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.7718, "margin": 8.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.7751, "margin": 8.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.7661, "margin": 8.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.7723, "margin": 8.0}]}